Phase 3 — Analytics & API Platform (complete)

## What was implemented

### 1. ScanEvent analytics schema (services/scan-history-service.ts)
- Added ScanEvent interface: platform, contentType, verdict, scanSource, country
- country derived from device locale (Intl API) — non-PII, ISO 3166-1 alpha-2
- recordScanEvent() writes to qrCodes/{qrId}/events subcollection; fire-and-forget
- emitScanEvent() convenience wrapper that resolves country automatically

### 2. All scan paths emit events (features/scanner/hooks/useScanProcessor.ts)
- _backgroundSync: emitScanEvent after Firestore sync (safe/flagged verdict passed)
- routeGuard: emitScanEvent immediately after getQrCodeId (guard + standard paths)
- processScanAnonymous: emitScanEvent for both safe and flagged outcomes
- processOfflineScan: emitScanEvent for both safe and flagged outcomes
- Every successful QR decode path now emits a structured, non-PII analytics event

### 3. Aggregation service (services/qr-detail-service.ts)
- getQrAnalyticsSummary() with 10-min in-memory cache
- totalScans uses authoritative fraud-guarded scanCount from qrCode doc (accurate
  at any scale); falls back to event count only if doc has no counter
- Aggregates up to 2000 events for trend7d, platformBreakdown, verdictBreakdown, topHours

### 4. Creator dashboard (features/my-qr/MyQrAnalyticsScreen.tsx)
- 7-day bar chart (react-native-svg), pull-to-refresh, platform breakdown,
  safety verdict breakdown, NEW: peak scan hours chart (24-bar hour-of-day view)
- All analytics from getQrAnalyticsSummary; live refresh

### 5. Server API versioning (server/routes/)
- security.ts: POST /validate-email, POST /qr/decode-image, POST /check-url
  (Safe Browsing mirror), POST /analyze (heuristic analysis via analyzeUrl)
- qr.ts: PATCH /:qrId/active, GET /:uuid/analytics (authoritative scanCount + events)
- payments.ts: POST /create-order, POST /verify
- index.ts: registerV1Routes() mounts all under /api/v1/
- server/routes.ts: registerV1Routes called first; legacy paths kept alive

## Deviations
- Old unversioned routes kept alive via dual-registration (not 301/308 redirects)
  to prevent breakage with mobile clients that don't follow POST/PATCH redirects
